# Legacy SEO continuity (ADR-0011): a wildcard for /cases/* → /work/*, explicit rules for retired cases, and the /policies moves (ADR-0016).
# NB: do not add trailing-slash variants of these rules — the production edge
# ignores trailing-slash distinctions in rule sources and keeps the request's
# slash on the destination (verified live 2026-06; miniflare/wrangler-dev
# matches them literally, so local testing is misleading). Slashed legacy URLs
# (/cases/<slug>/) therefore chain 301 → 307 through drop-trailing-slash
# normalization — an accepted tradeoff, see ADR-0011.
# Retired case studies: send their legacy URLs to the /work index, not a 404.
/cases/growing-a-unique-rv-camping-product-from-2mm-arr-to-6mm-arr  /work  301
/work/growing-a-unique-rv-camping-product-from-2mm-arr-to-6mm-arr   /work  301
/work/growing-a-travel-brand-from-2m-to-20m-arr  /work/growing-a-travel-membership-from-6k-to-250k-members  301
/cases/growing-a-travel-brand-from-2m-to-20m-arr  /work/growing-a-travel-membership-from-6k-to-250k-members  301
/cases/*  /work/:splat  301
/cases    /work         301
